  "status": "PROVED ROW-LOCAL CERTIFIER: COMPLETE NORMALIZED PAIR SIEVE MATCHES REPLAY KEYS",
  "task": "X73 h=4 normalized pair sieve",
  "theorem": "For p == 1 mod n, p not dividing n, Phi_n splits over F_p as the simple product over primitive n-th roots zeta^u.  Therefore a normalized word X+X^r-X^s-1 is p-norm-gated iff it vanishes at zeta^u for some unit u.  Enumerating every filtered normalized pair (1,r,s), applying this primitive-root test, and grouping survivors by the X68 key gives the complete row-local certifier key set.  In the replay rows this complete sieve matches exactly the keys obtained independently from finite-field X60 triples."
}
